        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1065c5d9-ef4b-5faa-9309-49e635166fc9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Equestria\n- Organizations: Hasbro\n- Products: Hasbro's animated show, its feature film\n- Peoples: unicorns, pegasi, earth ponies\n- Concepts: Wendigo psychosis, culture-bound syndrome\n- Characters: Wendigos, Ithaqua\n- Topics: Cthulhu Mythos, H. P. Lovecraft\n\nFacts:\n- Equestria is the primary setting for Hasbro's animated show and its feature film.\n- Equestria was founded when the three pony tribes—unicorns, pegasi, and earth ponies—came together in harmony to fight the Wendigos and stop an eternal blizzard.\n- Wendigo psychosis is a controversial modern medical term that psychiatrists have described as a culture-bound syndrome involving an intense craving for human flesh and a fear of becoming a cannibal.\n- Ithaqua, also called the Wind-Walker or the Wendigo, is a fictional character in H. P. Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "aa98af93-d49c-5f9f-bd56-d084aee32e19",
        "text": "Page: Equestria. Sentence: The Kingdom of Equestria, or simply, Equestria, is the primary setting for Hasbro's animated show, \"\", and its feature film \"\".\nPage: Equestria. Sentence: The nation was founded when the three pony tribes, unicorns, pegasi, and earth ponies, came together to in harmony, to fight the Wendigos, and to stop an eternal blizzard.\nPage: Wendigo. Sentence: The legend lends its name to the controversial modern medical term Wendigo psychosis, described by psychiatrists as a culture-bound syndrome with symptoms such as an intense craving for human flesh and a fear of becoming a cannibal.\nPage: Ithaqua. Sentence: Ithaqua (the \"Wind-Walker\" or the \"Wendigo\") is a fictional character in the Cthulhu Mythos of H. P. Lovecraft.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
